---
title: Rapido Mussels
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

Clean the @mussels{1%kg}(or any mix of clams, cockles, oysters, or other shellfish) washing them in running water; scrape the shell of any incrustations and pull off the "feathery" bit. Wash them again changing the water a couple of times.

Warm the @tomato purée{2%tbsp} in a large pan, add the @stock{6%tbsp}(or water, white wine, or cider), @madras curry powder{0.5%tsp}, @lemongrass{1%stem} and @fresh ginger{} cut into strips. Bring to the boil.

Add the shellfish to the tomato and cook on a high heat until they open (usually 1.5 to ~{5%minutes}) mixing occasionally.

Remove the shellfish and keep warm.

Add the @coconut milk{4%tbsp} and @garlic{3%cloves}(crushed) to the remaining sauce and bring to the boil. Adjust the seasoning with @salt and @pepper.

Remove from the heat, add the @mixed herbs{small bunch}(coriander, basil, flat parsley) and shellfish, mix and leave to infuse for at least ~{3%minutes} before serving.

Serve with a fork (for the mussels) and a spoon (for the marinade), optionally with bread.